* Thu Nov 19 2026 Brian G <justlostintime@gmail.com> 1.8.4
- Version 1.8 manual: help.info, manual.md and the wiki made consistent with gsh, new GambasShell-gsh-1.8 docx and pdf
- $0 $1..$n $# $* $@ work as in bash, the script name is only $0, $* is joined with spaces, $@ works on cli lines
- cli lines no longer see the parameters shifted by one ($0 was lambda.tmp)
- $! is the process id of the last background job, it was the id of gsh
- background programs are compiled by gb.scripter and run directly, gbs3 is no longer used
- kill $! also stops the command the background program started
- gsh -u runs a compiled script, compiled scripts start with #!/usr/bin/env -S gsh -u -- instead of gbs3
- &| &|> &|< pipe stdout and stderr together
- a misplaced pipe, && or || gives a clear error instead of Out of bounds or Unknown operator
- jobs records the end of every background job, with several running only one was recorded
- --single and --dictsize option names, $UID, onexit reload date check and --help spelling fixed
- ExecProg.gbs is saved only at trace level 20
- dbsave and dbload default to the gsh image, dbload no longer clears memory when the image file is missing
- nerdmode has a default, the unused nerdfont variable is removed
- jobs shows the command line of a background job, it showed the last history entry (exit in a script)
- jobs handles a command line containing |, it failed with Type mismatch
- errors inside a block no longer print the error location, it is still written to gsh.log
- clearsubs --NoSave works, the option was documented but not recognised
- the output of a sub run in the background is no longer lost when gsh writes to a pipe or a file

